<section class="p-hero"><div class="p-hero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/inspector.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/inspector-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/inspector.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.15"></div><div class="wrap p-hero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/claim-calculators/">Calculators</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Appraisal Readiness Checkup</span></nav><p class="kicker">Free checklist</p><h1>Appraisal Readiness Checkup: Is Your Claim File Ready?</h1><p class="lede">Strong appraisals are built before the demand letter goes out. Answer twelve quick questions to see where your file stands and what to fix first.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Appraisal readiness checkup</span><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation of what is covered. If the claim was denied outright, talk to a Pennsylvania attorney before considering appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask in writing for the complete itemized estimate, not just the payment summary."><span>Do you have the carrier’s full, line-item estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get a line-item estimate from a contractor or estimator; a one-line bid won’t carry weight with a panel."><span>Do you have your own itemized estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Find the ‘Suit Against Us’ condition (often one year in Pennsylvania policies) and put the date on your calendar."><span>Do you know your policy’s suit-limitation date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Collect every photo and video, note the dates, and add photos of current conditions."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Appraisal’ paragraph in the conditions section and note any time limits for naming an appraiser."><span>Have you read the appraisal clause in your policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Tarp, dry out or board up as needed and keep every receipt."><span>Have temporary repairs been made, with receipts saved?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure wet walls, attics, decking and party walls have been checked so the scope is complete."><span>Has hidden damage been opened up and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the numbers in the claim gap & fee projector; a small gap may not justify appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap more than roughly 10% or $5,000?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request the declarations page that was in force on the date of loss."><span>Do you have your current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Put letters, emails and claim notes in date order."><span>Is your correspondence with the carrier organized by date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="If a proof of loss was requested, complete it and keep proof of delivery."><span>If the carrier asked for a sworn proof of loss, was it returned on time?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out tool-out-score" aria-live="polite">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#E4E9F5" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#FFCE00" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3" style="transition:stroke-dashoffset .5s,stroke .3s"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul class="todo" data-o="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div>
<p class="tool-note">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms; they aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice. Nothing you type is stored or sent.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>How the checkup is weighted</h2>
<p>Coverage, estimates and the suit-limitation date carry the most weight because they decide whether appraisal is the right tool at all and whether you have time to use it. Paperwork items still matter, but they are easier to fix.</p>
<h2>What to do with your score</h2>
<ul><li><strong>75 or higher:</strong> your file is in good shape. A professional review of the gap is the logical next step.</li>
<li><strong>45 to 74:</strong> close the open items first; each one strengthens your number.</li>
<li><strong>Below 45:</strong> demanding appraisal now could lock in a low award. Build the file first.</li></ul>

<h2>Questions about this calculator</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is anything I enter saved or sent?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. The checkup runs entirely in your browser and nothing is stored.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I share my results with an appraiser?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Take a screenshot or copy your to-do list and bring it to a consultation.</p></div></details></div>
